  "details": "A comprehensive list for all the supported unicode would be very helpful.\nUnicode is a great way to allow players to have unique names. Since you can only change your name once every three months, the only way to safely check if a unicode is supported by VRC is to change your name in Styou. log in with your steam acct in VRC, and check when it says \"Logging in as ______\". If you fully log in and check your name in social, your name is listed as your VRC name so you can only see the steam name change in the logging in screen.\nIf the unicode is supported, and for example I wanted a ° degree symbol in my name, I would see \"Logging in as Ghost°\" but if it wasn't supported, I would see \"Logging in as Ghost \"\nI have to do this for every symbol I want to check and its a slow and tedious process. I am not willing to try this with the vr chat home name editor since if the website allows the change but the unicode isn't supported then I have to wait 3 months to change it again, and I will have a name with invisible characters.\nPlease consider making a list of all unicode supported by VRC, Thank you.",
